ot; well to me though. While I could list dozens of great actors that fit (some of whom are not names that come to mind with the phrase &quot;old school&quot;), the people it cuts off is weird to me... since Harrison Ford and Morgan Freeman don't fit that (while for different reasons and under different circumstances, both had other jobs as adults before becoming full time actors, so they haven't been acting their entire adult lives).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T17:53:00-08:00","id":1546615,"title":"","content":"Just pulling a loose definition out of thin air of &quot;anyone older than I am who was acting in the 1970s or earlier ...<br /> <br /> I think Timothy Dalton was highly underrated as James Bond, especially in The Living Daylights. But also his work in The Lion in Winter, Cromwell, Flash Gordon, The Rocketeer, and Hot Fuzz. <br /> <br /> Also Kurt Douglas (20000 Leagues Under the Sea, Spartacus, Lust for Life, The Indian Fighter, and many others).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T18:21:50-08:00","id":1546617,"title":"","content":"Kirk Douglas I remember him from Spartacus, War Wagon, Tough Guys and Gunfight at the O.K. Corral.<br /> <br /> I could never warm up to Timothy Dalton as James Bond, but I felt Pierce Brosnan was a great James Bond that didn't have great material to work from and after the Bourne Identity did better in terms of box office success. The folks behind Double 007 had to do that reboot with Daniel Craig and I felt he was a great Bond and I couldn't see what the issue people had with his last time at bat.<br /> <br /> Roger Moore last go around as James Bond In View To A Kill was bad all around and even Moore said he shouldn't have done that film at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}